WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.535 --> 00:00:16.869
After Father returned home, Beth's recovery took a turn for the better as she rapidly grew stronger.

2
00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:21.243
In no time she was climbing upstairs and downstairs on her own.

3
00:00:21.244 --> 00:00:25.936
Being with his family again seemed to have the same effect on Father's health as well.

4
00:00:25.937 --> 00:00:34.504
True, he had lost a lot of weight and his body seemed stiff and sore, but his eyes remained as kind and watchful as ever.

5
00:00:34.505 --> 00:00:37.997
"Shall I continue with the next chapter, or do you want a nap?"

6
00:00:37.998 --> 00:00:41.607
Father asked Beth, who was lying on the sofa listening to him read.

7
00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:48.109
Jo, who was also listening, answered excitedly, "Please carry on. I want to know what happens!"

8
00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:56.721
Laughing, Beth nodded and said, "I'd like to hear more, too, Father, but only if you're not too tired."

9
00:00:56.722 --> 00:01:03.490
"I never get tired of reading to you, my dear girl," Father said lovingly, as he turned the page and continued.

10
00:01:03.491 --> 00:01:08.759
"Oh, this color is not right either!" complained Amy from the corner by the window,

11
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.941
where she had set up her easel and was trying to paint a vase of flowers.

12
00:01:12.942 --> 00:01:21.089
Mother and Meg, smiled at the peacefulness of their family at that moment. But the peace didn't last long.

13
00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:26.985
"Oh, I can't believe she's here!" Amy suddenly cried as she glanced out the window.

14
00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:31.322
"Who, Amy?" asked Mother, standing up to look for herself.

15
00:01:31.323 --> 00:01:39.085
"Aunt March! Thank goodness, she didn't bring that annoying parrot," said Amy, screwing the lids back on her paints.

16
00:01:39.086 --> 00:01:47.627
Unseen by their children, Mother and Father exchanged wordless glances that meant "get ready" for this unexpected visit.

17
00:01:47.628 --> 00:01:52.428
Mother opened the door for Aunt March as she strolled into the house as if she owned it.

18
00:01:52.429 --> 00:01:57.226
"Oh, there you are," she said, catching sight of Father.

19
00:01:57.227 --> 00:02:02.903
"How are you, Aunt?" he asked graciously as he stood to give her a kiss on the cheek.

20
00:02:02.904 --> 00:02:08.442
"You go off to war at your age, get sick, take away the children's mother,

21
00:02:08.443 --> 00:02:14.353
meanwhile your small one gets scarlet fever and nearly dies," snapped Aunt March,

22
00:02:14.354 --> 00:02:20.686
"so that the youngest, as adorable as she is"—here Aunt March nodded approvingly at Amy—

23
00:02:20.687 --> 00:02:28.971
"is sent over to my care despite my illnesses . . . and you ask me how I am!" she concluded.

24
00:02:28.972 --> 00:02:36.900
While Father tried to explain his situation to Aunt March, who demanded that Jo bring a blanket for her cold knees and ordered hot tea from Meg,

25
00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:39.710
Amy announced more visitors to the house.

26
00:02:39.711 --> 00:02:45.329
"Here come Laurie and Mr. Brookes," she shouted, waving eagerly out the window.

27
00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:50.030
Cheeks flushing, Meg quickly disappeared into the kitchen to get the tea.

28
00:02:50.031 --> 00:02:57.331
Father stood up, relieved, even for a moment, not to have to listen to his aunt's scolding, and welcomed the guests into his home.

29
00:02:57.332 --> 00:03:05.647
Father and Mr. Brookes had formed a close bond during his sickness, and since then Mr. Brookes had become a regular visitor to the March home.

30
00:03:05.648 --> 00:03:12.159
As much as Meg tried to appear cool, secretly, she was happy to see John so often.

31
00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.696
Her pride might not admit it, but Meg's heart could no longer deny her feelings for him.

32
00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:24.308
"I have something to ask you, sir," Mr. Brookes said to Father, not realizing that Aunt March was there.

33
00:03:24.309 --> 00:03:27.852
"Who are you?" asked Aunt March bluntly.

34
00:03:27.853 --> 00:03:36.172
While Father explained, Meg entered with the tea, her hands shaking ever so slightly, causing the china to rattle on the tray.

35
00:03:36.173 --> 00:03:44.538
"Child," Aunt March shrieked at Meg, "I swear you're going to break that cheap tea set if you clink them any harder!"

36
00:03:44.539 --> 00:03:51.784
Turning a deep red, Meg would have dropped the tray if Mr. Brookes hadn't sprung up and taken it from her trembling hands.

37
00:03:51.785 --> 00:03:58.578
As Aunt March sipped her tea, she kept one eye on Mr. Brookes, sensing his obvious attraction to Meg,

38
00:03:58.579 --> 00:04:04.549
and the other eye on Meg, who undoubtedly shared the same feelings toward him.

39
00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:10.616
Meanwhile Jo, oblivious to what was happening, caught sight of Laurie trying to get her attention.

40
00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:15.687
He motioned with his head toward the kitchen, so Jo cautiously got up and crept away.

41
00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.027
Laurie joined her a few minutes later.

42
00:04:18.028 --> 00:04:20.716
"What is it?" Jo asked him.

43
00:04:20.717 --> 00:04:27.049
"Something major is about to happen. I can't tell you but . . . ," Laurie began excitedly.

44
00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:31.744
"Then why bother calling me into the kitchen?" Jo asked irritably.

45
00:04:31.745 --> 00:04:35.559
"To save you the shock," Laurie said.

46
00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:38.188
"From what?" asked Jo.

47
00:04:38.189 --> 00:04:46.263
"Something major is going to happen that will change your life forever," Laurie said firmly, looking deep into Jo's eyes.

48
00:04:46.264 --> 00:04:54.332
Then grabbing her arm, he led her back to the living room, where to Jo's horror, the big event was just taking place.

49
00:04:54.333 --> 00:04:58.665
Mr. Brookes was on his knee in front of Meg and he was holding her hand.

50
00:04:58.666 --> 00:05:03.641
"Margaret March, will you marry me?" Brookes asked in a gentlemanly manner.

51
00:05:03.642 --> 00:05:07.784
"What is the meaning of this?" Aunt March demanded.

52
00:05:07.785 --> 00:05:11.751
"This is an outrage! You are only a child!"

53
00:05:11.752 --> 00:05:16.713
"Aunt March, I don't think this matter concerns you," Father said firmly.

54
00:05:16.714 --> 00:05:21.351
"Of course it concerns me! I am the head of the family.

55
00:05:21.352 --> 00:05:27.240
You belong to me! Therefore I have a right to speak!" she said haughtily.

56
00:05:27.241 --> 00:05:34.602
"I love your grand-niece, madam, and I promise to make her as happy and content as she is now," John said kindly.

57
00:05:34.603 --> 00:05:43.458
Looking him up and down, Aunt March said disdainfully, "You're nothing but a poor tutor. How can you make this girl happy?"

58
00:05:43.459 --> 00:05:49.024
Poor Mr. Brookes flushed with embarrassment and anger, but he controlled it admirably.

59
00:05:49.025 --> 00:05:52.045
Surprisingly, it was Meg who spoke up.

60
00:05:52.046 --> 00:05:56.996
"Aunt March! I will not allow you to speak to this man in that way.

61
00:05:56.997 --> 00:06:03.773
He is a good kind person who has helped our family when we needed him. What have you done for us?

62
00:06:03.774 --> 00:06:08.604
You never offered to help Father when he lost his money or even when he was sick.

63
00:06:08.605 --> 00:06:12.036
You never came to visit Beth while she had the fever.

64
00:06:12.037 --> 00:06:18.476
And now you come here and tell me that I can't marry the man who has done nothing but good for our family?

65
00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:24.946
No! I will not allow it!" Meg cried, not caring as tears rolled down her cheeks.

66
00:06:24.947 --> 00:06:30.502
Everyone was stunned. They had never seen Meg react so strongly in her life.

67
00:06:30.503 --> 00:06:35.400
Shaking with anger, Aunt March pointed her walking stick at Meg and threatened,

68
00:06:35.401 --> 00:06:44.457
"I warn you, Margaret, if you marry this man, you will not get a single penny from me when I die!"

69
00:06:44.458 --> 00:06:52.456
Meg took a deep breath and turning her back on Aunt March, she grabbed John's hands and said to him, "Yes, John Brookes, I will marry you."

70
00:06:52.457 --> 00:07:00.916
Jo felt the ground drop from beneath her and before she knew it, she was lying on the floor with a circle of worried faces staring down at her.

71
00:07:00.917 --> 00:07:06.617
"Are you all right, Jo?" Laurie asked, pulling Jo up and giving her a slight shake.

72
00:07:06.618 --> 00:07:11.122
Nodding, Jo said, "Yes, I'm fine."

73
00:07:11.123 --> 00:07:20.739
"Oh, Jo, isn't this wonderful news?" Meg said in a breathless voice as she hugged her sister. "I'm getting married!"

74
00:07:20.746 --> 00:07:32.044
Hearing those words again, Jo fainted. She hoped she would never wake up from the awful nightmare that was about to unfold.
